[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865171769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106192#issuecomment-2865171769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106192","id":2865171769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qxw05","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T05:29:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T05:46:12Z","body":"I found a ZDoom forum post where using a compositor was the solution to getting VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, which made me remember that I disabled the compositor on my laptop because having it on made Godot run so poorly. In the next couple of days I will see if re-enabling the compositor stop the crashes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865171769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875155899","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106192#issuecomment-2875155899","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106192","id":2875155899,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rX2W7","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T06:05:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T06:05:33Z","body":"So I enabled a compositor, but the crashes persisted. This time I actually got a crash while the editor was focused. I'm using XFCE and I was trying picom to fix the issue, neither of which I'm using on my desktop. I'm also not using Mint on my desktop. I may try installing a different distro on my laptop at some point to see if it fixes the issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875155899/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888287552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106192#issuecomment-2888287552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106192","id":2888287552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJ8VA","user":{"login":"mechalynx","id":8427257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjcyNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8427257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx","html_url":"https://github.com/mechalynx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T10:45:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T10:47:55Z","body":"This is unlikely to help but for what it's worth, it is the case for _AMD_ internal graphics that certain combinations of motherboard and RAM can cause the device to be lost occasionally. For me this happened in Overwatch only: using the 5600G internal graphics and compatible RAM in XMP mode, it would sometimes crash with a \"rendering device lost\" message (I don't remember the exact wording). In that case, it was fixable by increasing the CAS latency from 16 to 18 and it never happened again.\n\nI know you have an Intel CPU and I only know of this happening in that specific generation of _AMD_ internal GPUs due to the RAM latency on some RAM sticks only but it might be worth trying, just in case. I would keep expectations low though.\n\nIf indeed it makes a difference however, it would be useful to know as troubleshooting information for internal GPUs both for the editor and released games.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888287552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888790152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106192#issuecomment-2888790152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106192","id":2888790152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sL3CI","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-18T05:55:11Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T05:55:28Z","body":"@mechalynx Unfortunately while this could be of use to someone else, I'm pretty certain that my laptop's bios doesn't have any options related to memory. Thanks for the suggestion though. I did install a single 8gb dimm alongside the 4gb soldered to the board but removing it and only having 4gb of memory reduces usability significantly, especially when sharing it with the igpu.\n\nOne thing that I thought about since creating this issue is that I used 4.3 a fair bit on this laptop and I don't remember having this problem. From what I recall it only seemed to start happening after either 4.4 or 4.4.1, and I didn't change anything else about the laptop in that time, I don't think I even updated the packages since using 4.3 until I tried to fix this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888790152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2889077084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106192#issuecomment-2889077084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106192","id":2889077084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sM9Fc","user":{"login":"mechalynx","id":8427257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjcyNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8427257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx","html_url":"https://github.com/mechalynx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-18T16:15:26Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T16:16:45Z","body":"My mind went to Wayland support but it seems this was already in by 4.4/4.4.1. What has changed is the embedded game window support, which was added in 4.4 I think. I don't think it's on by default though, so I'm not sure how you could have run into an issue due to that.\n\nPerhaps you could also try single window mode if you haven't already, though again there's only a small change that'll change anything.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2889077084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]